# GitQuest Lab: Build a Full-Screen, Interactive Git Learning Platform

## 1. Your role and mission

Act as a senior product designer, frontend architect, Git expert, and experienced React engineer.

Transform my existing GitQuest Lab project into a premium, scenario-driven Git learning platform where users learn Git by seeing it, experimenting with commands, understanding repository changes, and practising on their own computers.

This is an existing project that needs a substantial improvement in its user experience and functionality. Inspect the current code before making changes. Preserve working functionality where appropriate, but do not let the existing UI limit the redesign.

The product must support:

- Beginner-friendly Git fundamentals.
- Interactive command execution inside a browser-based Git simulator.
- Visual explanations of Git repository states and commit history.
- Local and remote repository workflows.
- Real-world troubleshooting scenarios.
- All 80 questions in the supplied Git interview preparation guide.
- Real-machine exercises for Windows, macOS, and Linux.
- Learning progress and revision.
- Production deployment on Vercel.

The core learning loop is:

**Learn → Visualize → Execute → Inspect → Practise → Verify.**

Do not build a static documentation website or a dashboard full of decorative cards. Build a working Git learning environment.

